      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "HCF (Highest Common Factor) is the greatest divisor shared by given numbers.",
        "LCM (Least Common Multiple) is the smallest positive integer divisible by all given numbers.",
        "For any two given numbers, Product of Numbers = HCF × LCM.",
        "HCF of Fractions = HCF of Numerators / LCM of Denominators.",
        "LCM of Fractions = LCM of Numerators / HCF of Denominators."
      ],
      "id": "zvamhzb"
    },
